    <DataNode elementId="AT5G26570-MONOMER" textLabel="phosphoglucan, water dikinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q6ZY51" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">|FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| (phosphoglucan, water dikinase) is a plastidial enzyme that plays a crucial role in starch degradation |CITS: [19325165]|. By phosphorylating the hydroxyl group on the C3 carbon of glucosyl residues in |FRAME: 6-Phosphogluco-Starches 6-phosphogluco-starch|, |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| appears to promote starch solubilization |CITS: [19325165]|. In &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; experiments, |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| only acts on the model substrate crystalline |FRAME: Maltodextrins maltodextrin| after this glucan has been pre-phosphorylated by |FRAME: AT1G10760-MONOMER GWD|. For this presumed slightly disorderd crystalline |FRAME: Poly-6-Phosphogluco-Maltodextrins poly-6-phosphogluco maltodextrin| substrate, |FRAME: AT5G26570-MONOMER PWD| has a specific activty of 2 nmol phosphate incorporated mg&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt; protein min&lt;sup&gt;-1&lt;/sup&gt;. Crystalline |FRAME: Maltodextrins maltodextrin| adopts a B-type allomorph, also found in the starch of Arabidopsis leaves, potato leaves, potato tubers, and amylose extender maize kernals and it is presumed that |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| will act on these starches after they have been acted on by a glucan, water dikinase like |FRAME: AT1G10760-MONOMER GWD| |CITS: [19325165][18419779]|. Within glucan chains, this enzymes seems to prefer phosphorylating the hydroxyl group on the C3 carbon of glucose |CITS: [16914145][15618411][15686522]|. |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| mRNA is expressed throughout the plant. PWD activity &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; is expected to be high during the night when transitory starch reserves created during photosynthesis in the leaf are broken down to form usable sugars, such as |FRAME: SUCROSE sucrose|. Consistent with this model, there is evidence that both |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| and |FRAME: AT1G10760-MONOMER GWD| mRNA levels peak at the end of the light period, however, there is no evidence that the |FRAME: AT1G10760-MONOMER GWD| protein levels change throughout the day |CITS: [11487701]| and it is not clear whether |FRAME: AT5G25670-MONOMER PWD| protein levels fluctuate diurnally. The biological activity of this enzyme &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; is supported by the phenotype of plants with downregulated PWD activity that have an overall elevation in the level of starch, but a reduced level of glucose-3-phosphate in their starch |CITS: [15686522][15618411]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G26570-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G26570.1" />
